# Topics for Pong P. Chu, FPGA Prototyping by VHDL Examples, Xilinx
# Spartan-3 version (Wiley, 2008): which pages are about which Wire example,
# chip or part. The page numbers are those of the PDF (the e-book), not the
# numbers printed on the pages.
#
#   page[-last]  Title of the section  :  patterns
#
# A pattern is an example's file name, a chip (component) name, or a part
# kind (dff, mux, ram ...); * matches anything. The first section that
# matches is the page opened; the others are listed under the book.
#
# The book is not part of Wire: open your own copy with Open PDF.
#
# Two parts: first the listings (each example's own code), then every
# section of the book from its table of contents. A section with nothing
# after the colon is in the book's Contents but no part leads to it.

